---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Getting Started">
	<h1>Getting Started</h1>
	<p>
		This is a second, fully static page — no islands, no client JS at all. It exists to show
		Astro's file-based routing: <code>src/pages/docs/getting-started.astro</code> maps directly
		to <code>/docs/getting-started</code>.
	</p>

	<h2>How this site is put together</h2>
	<pre><code>src/
  layouts/BaseLayout.astro   — shared shell, all pages render inside this
  components/ScoreEstimator.tsx — the one React island, hydrated with client:visible
  pages/index.astro          — landing page + the island
  pages/docs/getting-started.astro — this page, pure static HTML</code></pre>

	<h2>Content vs. interactivity</h2>
	<p>
		Astro ships zero JavaScript by default and only hydrates a component when a page
		explicitly asks for it via a <code>client:*</code> directive. That's the split this
		project demonstrates: static, content-first pages by default, with a React component
		opted into hydration only where the page genuinely needs state.
	</p>
</BaseLayout>
